\tag{fdip}
\title{Rotation transport on a fixed torus}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{There are two exterior factors: one records the directions of a
cubical cell, and one is its internal coefficient. Rotational links
act on the second. Keeping these factors distinct permits the
transport and its adjoint to be computed directly, even when the
group of allowed rotations is infinite.}

\transclude{fdip-00YM}
